April O'Neil (voice), played by Sarah Michelle Gellar.

10
00:36:15,000 --> 00:36:21,000
Casey Jones (voice), played by Chris Evans.

11
00:39:52,500 --> 00:39:58,500
TMNT (abbreviated from Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles) is a 2007 animated superhero film written and directed by Kevin
Munroe in his feature directorial debut and based on the characters created by Peter Laird and Kevin Eastman.

12
00:43:30,000 --> 00:43:36,000
The first animated film in the franchise, it features the voices of Chris Evans, Sarah Michelle Gellar,
Mako, Kevin Smith, Patrick Stewart, and Ziyi Zhang with narration by Laurence Fishburne.

13
00:47:07,500 --> 00:47:13,500
In the film, after having grown apart following the final defeat of their arch-enemy, the Shredder, the four Turtles — Leonardo, Raphael, Donatello, and Michelangelo (voiced respectively
by James Arnold Taylor, Nolan North, Mitchell Whitfield, and Mikey Kelley) — are set to reunite and overcome their faults to save the world from evil ancient creatures.

14
00:50:45,000 --> 00:50:51,000
Development and pre-production for TMNT began in June 2005 at Imagi's Los Angeles facility and
the animation was produced in Hong Kong, followed by post-production in Hollywood.

15
00:54:22,500 --> 00:54:28,500
Munroe chose to produce the film in CGI animation as opposed to live-action like the prior Turtles
films, in an effort to make it easier for audiences to suspend their disbelief.

16
00:58:00,000 --> 00:58:06,000
When writing the film, Munroe wanted to divert away from the lighthearted elements of the
franchise and put a heavier emphasis on the darker tone of the original comics.

17
01:01:37,500 --> 01:01:43,500
The animators that worked on the fight sequences were
inspired by Hong Kong action films.

18
01:05:15,000 --> 01:05:21,000
TMNT premiered at the Grauman's Chinese Theatre in Los Angeles on March 17, 2007, and was
released theatrically in the United States on March 23, by Warner Bros.

19
01:08:52,500 --> 01:08:58,500
Pictures, it was released in Hong Kong on March 29 by Golden Scene, and
internationally distributed by The Weinstein Company.

20
01:12:30,000 --> 01:12:36,000
The film received mixed reviews from critics, but was a small commercial success,
grossing $95.6 million worldwide against a $34 million production budget.

21
01:16:07,500 --> 01:16:13,500
Planned sequels were cancelled after Nickelodeon acquired the franchise in
2009, rebooting the film series with a live-action film in 2014.

22
01:19:45,000 --> 01:19:51,000
The film explores themes of new york city, journalist,
martial arts, sibling relationship, skateboarding.

23
01:23:22,500 --> 01:23:28,500
The tone is lighthearted.
